Package: mds.setup.check
Type: Project
Title: R Dependencies For The MDS Setup Check
Version: 0.1.0
Description: This project is not an R package, and STUDENTS NEVER TOUCH THIS FILE.
    Their R packages come from the library the MDS install guides set up; renv is not
    mentioned in orientation and the assignment handouts contain no lock file of any
    kind. This exists for CI and for anyone rebuilding the repository from a clean
    clone.
    .
    It lets renv take an *explicit* snapshot: the packages below are declared here
    rather than inferred by scanning the code for library() calls. Inference was
    quietly wrong here -- ggplot2 is loaded by an assignment that renv scanned but CI
    never rendered, so it never reached renv.lock and a clean clone could not have
    built the R lab. What each one is for:
    .
    rmarkdown renders check-rmarkdown.Rmd through R itself, which is one of the two
    routes the README's matrix measures for that fixture.
    .
    knitr is the engine Quarto uses for every .Rmd and .qmd with an R chunk. It
    arrives with rmarkdown anyway; it is named because Quarto calls it directly and a
    reader should not have to know that rmarkdown depends on it.
    .
    ggplot2 draws the figure in section 3 of mds-demo-assignment/source/lab0b. It is
    part of the tidyverse, which the MDS install guides put on every student machine,
    so students already have it. This entry is only so CI and a fresh clone can build
    the lab as well.
    .
    ottr is the R autograder. Students run ottr::check() in the lab, and the install
    guides check for it by name.
    .
    testthat is what the ottr tests are written in (testthat::expect_equal and the
    like). It arrives with ottr, and is named for the same reason as knitr.
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    ggplot2,
    knitr,
    ottr,
    renv,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat
